        "text": "6 : 5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Areas with a common apex",
        "body": "Let the area of $ABC$ be 4, so each small triangle has area 1. F and D lie on $BA$, E on $CA$.\n\n- Triangles $CBF$ and $CBA$ have the same height from C, so $\\frac{BF}{BA} = \\frac14$, hence $AF = \\frac34 BA$.\n- Triangle $CFA$ has area 3 and $CFE$ has area 1, so $CE = \\frac13 CA$; triangle $EFA$ has area 2.\n- In triangle $EFA$, triangles $EFD$ and $EDA$ both have area 1 and the same height from E, so D is the midpoint of $FA$: $FD = \\frac38 BA$.\n\nThen $BD = BF + FD = \\frac14 BA + \\frac38 BA = \\frac58 BA$, and $AF : BD = \\frac68 : \\frac58 = 6 : 5$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 6 : 5**"
      }
    ],
