    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Corner planes",
        "body": "Three vertices of a cube lie either on a face or on a diagonal rectangle through two opposite edges (each of these planes contains 4 vertices), or they are the three neighbours of one vertex. The plane through the three neighbours of a vertex cuts off that corner and contains no other vertex. There is one such plane for each of the 8 vertices, so the answer is 8.\n\n**Answer: (D) 8**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count by complement",
        "body": "There are $\\binom83 = 56$ triples of vertices. The 6 faces and 6 diagonal rectangles contain 4 vertices each, i.e. $12\\cdot\\binom43 = 48$ triples. The remaining $56 - 48 = 8$ triples each determine their own plane with exactly three vertices: 8 planes.\n\n**Answer: (D) 8**"
      }
    ],
