      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Find a",
        "body": "A number with exactly 4 divisors is $p^3$ or $pq$ ($p \\ne q$ primes).\n\n- If $3a = 3q$ with a prime $q \\neq 3$, then $a = q$ and $5a = 5q$ has 3 divisors ($q = 5$) or 4 divisors — never 6.\n- So $3a = p^3$, which forces $p = 3$ and $a = 9$. Check: $5a = 45 = 3^2\\cdot 5$ has $(2+1)(1+1) = 6$ divisors ✓.\n\nThen $2019a = 2019\\cdot 9 = 18171$, whose first digit is **1**.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1**"
      }
    ],
