      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the diagonal",
        "body": "The overlap region is symmetric about both diagonals, so the largest circle is centred at the centre O of the square. The quarter circle around S has radius 2, and O is at distance $\\sqrt2$ (half the diagonal) from S. So the circle around O can have radius $2 - \\sqrt2$ before touching that arc (and by symmetry the other one). Its area is $\\pi(2 - \\sqrt2)^2 = \\pi(4 - 4\\sqrt2 + 2) = (6 - 4\\sqrt2)\\pi$.\n\n**Answer: (E) $(6 - 4\\sqrt2)\\pi$**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check the size",
        "body": "$(6 - 4\\sqrt2)\\pi \\approx 0.34\\cdot 3.14 \\approx 1.08$, a reasonable area for a circle of radius about $0.59$ in a square of area 4. Option (A) would be about $9.97$, larger than the square; (B) is negative.\n\n**Answer: (E) $(6 - 4\\sqrt2)\\pi$**"
      }
    ],
